    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with significant upside, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), who occupies the prime leadoff spot against Phillips. His elite speed metrics are fully leveraged here, bolstered by a 10% efficiency bump from the #1 spot and a favorable platoon matchup. **Christian Yelich** (74.33) and **Yordan Alvarez** (71.69) follow closely, both benefitting from high-leverage lineup positions and favorable matchups against Singer and Rodriguez respectively. While **Yordan Alvarez** faces a slight penalty for the L/L matchup, his xwOBA profile remains too dominant to suppress, and **Christian Yelich** continues to thrive against RHP, providing a massive boost to our daily output.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card involved the utility spot, where **Junior Caminero** (61.33) narrowly edged out **Pedro Ramirez** (49.19). While **Pedro Ramirez** posted a respectable 49.19, he remains a tier below the primary starters, as the model preferred the established top-of-order security of **Junior Caminero** despite the challenge posed by Gore. Meanwhile, **Chase Meidroth** (54.04) maintains a marginal status; though we are awaiting official lineup confirmation, his projected placement at #7 against Ober keeps him in the lineup, though he is the most vulnerable to a late-inning replacement if the bench needs to be utilized to chase stolen bases.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the risk factors attached to today's rotation. **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (56.88) and **Chase Meidroth** (54.04) are operating near our threshold for viability, largely due to concerns regarding SP skill levels and platoon positioning. Notably, **Colt Keith** (46.34) was benched primarily due to the elite arm of Williams, whose sub-3.00 xERA significantly stifled the offensive projections. With stolen bases being the primary scarcity in this 5x5 Roto race, keep a close watch on **Caleb Durbin** (67.85) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**; their ability to manufacture runs via the base paths is the engine driving our competitive edge today.",
